spanmark/audio/atomic_wave_noise.py

  Deterministic timestamp-preserving impulse and stationary-noise atoms adapted
  from RawBoost, following SentryMao/SAL commit
  b4e80d1d2fd98f3d8b9a85a47837ab3a73e12485.

  Copyright (c) 2026 Yuchen Mao
  Copyright (c) 2021 Hemlata Tak et al.

  Both upstream projects distribute this code under the MIT license.

  Only two atoms are retained from RawBoost: the signal-dependent impulse and
  the stationary signal-independent noise. No filter is applied to the source
  waveform, so source samples are neither shifted nor mixed across label edges —
  which is what makes the augmentation safe for a localization task, where a
  moved sample is a moved label.

